Um, wow! Sure.

16:03.749 --> 16:05.042
Fantastic.

16:05.793 --> 16:07.211
What the hell was that for?

16:07.295 --> 16:09.675
Now we have the pot and the money.

16:10.965 --> 16:12.466
You sure this is gonna work, Peter?

16:12.552 --> 16:14.596
All I know is there's a lot of money
to be made

16:14.720 --> 16:17.471
in these stupid teen dramas
they keep putting on TV.

16:17.597 --> 16:19.099
And we're gonna get our share.

16:45.125 --> 16:47.669
<i>Come on, Joey. I wanna be with you.</i>

16:47.796 --> 16:50.465
<i>Dawson, I'm just not ready
to give up my virginity.</i>

16:50.590 --> 16:52.302
<i>- Come on.
- No!</i>

16:52.426 --> 16:55.094
<i>I promised myself
that I'd save it for the man that I marry.</i>

16:55.176 --> 16:56.679
<i>Come on. That's stupid.</i>

16:56.763 --> 16:59.309
<i>- I'm just not comfortable, you know?
- Well, I don't...</i>

16:59.434 --> 17:00.976
<i>This is, like, the '90s, man.</i>

17:01.101 --> 17:03.019
<i>I mean, like, everybody...</i>

17:03.103 --> 17:06.690
<i>Come on. You saw me on that boat.
I was wearing a blazer.</i>

17:07.189 --> 17:08.692
<i>- Come on.
- No! I just...</i>

17:08.817 --> 17:10.904
<i>I don't want to! All right?
I don't want to right now!</i>

17:11.028 --> 17:12.323
<i>I told you I'm not comfortable.</i>

17:12.448 --> 17:13.865
<i>I think you could respect that.</i>

17:13.948 --> 17:16.284
<i>- You know?
- I do respect. I totally respect it.</i>

17:16.367 --> 17:18.662
<i>That just makes me
want you more, you know?</i>

17:18.745 --> 17:21.496
<i>Come on, man. Let's just...
Let's just go nuts. Let's just...</i>

17:21.579 --> 17:23.792
<i>- No, I said... I don't...
- Come on!</i>

17:23.875 --> 17:26.585
<i>I don't want... No!
No! Peter, stop! Just stop! All right!</i>

17:26.710 --> 17:27.795
<i>Turn off the camera!</i>

17:27.878 --> 17:29.505
<i>God, I'm sorry, Mr. Pewterschmidt.</i>

17:29.589 --> 17:31.301
<i>I don't want to do this anymore, all right?</i>

17:31.383 --> 17:32.676
<i>You know what? You went too far.</i>

17:32.760 --> 17:34.093
<i>- What?
- You went too far.</i>

17:34.218 --> 17:35.345
<i>That's his character. That's how...</i>

17:35.428 --> 17:36.430
<i>I mean, he's that kind of...</i>

17:36.556 --> 17:37.556
<i>No! Forget it. Forget it.</i>

17:37.682 --> 17:38.931
<i>You know what? It's just weird, man.</i>

17:39.057 --> 17:40.142
<i>It's just weird. You're weird.</i>

17:40.226 --> 17:41.601
<i>All right? Just get off it.</i>

17:41.725 --> 17:43.854
<i>Let's just do something else
to make money.</i>

17:43.980 --> 17:45.521
<i>And we will be back.</i>

17:50.649 --> 17:52.864
Stand back, Brian.
I'm preparing for my vault.

17:52.988 --> 17:55.491
You can't vault inside the living room.
You're gonna get hurt.

17:55.574 --> 17:57.825
Yeah. I'll get hurt
right onto a Wheaties box.

17:57.909 --> 17:58.953
I don't see that happening.

17:59.079 --> 18:00.455
Yeah? Who cares what you say?

18:00.579 --> 18:02.749
You're a dog. You can't see colors.

18:02.875 --> 18:05.668
Which means you can't see the colors
of the American flag.

18:05.750 --> 18:06.836
Commie.

18:11.464 --> 18:13.552
I think I'm okay.

18:22.100 --> 18:24.229
Oh, God! Somebody!

18:24.353 --> 18:28.482
Do I take it out or do I leave it in?

18:30.359 --> 18:32.070
- Got it! We'll rob a train.
- Love it.

18:38.953 --> 18:40.204
All aboard.

18:43.289 --> 18:45.126
All right, everybody. This is a...

18:45.251 --> 18:46.586
Hey, where the hell is everybody?

18:46.711 --> 18:48.712
Oh, we haven't had
a paying customer in months.

18:48.795 --> 18:50.922
Nobody rides the train anymore.

18:51.048 --> 18:52.760
Oh, well, for God's sake!

18:53.717 --> 18:55.804
Are... Are you robbers?

18:55.928 --> 18:56.930
Yeah.

18:57.513 --> 18:59.099
Well, you could take my wallet.

18:59.224 --> 19:01.517
My MasterCard's in there.
Although, to be honest,

19:01.643 --> 19:04.563
I'll probably just cancel it
before you can use it. So...

19:04.647 --> 19:05.899
Oh, um...

19:07.606 --> 19:08.858
Give me that hole punch!

19:08.984 --> 19:10.777
Yeah!

19:10.902 --> 19:13.404
Is this your hole punch
or the train company's?

19:13.486 --> 19:14.656
Well, that's... You know what?

19:14.781 --> 19:15.908
I got to pay for that.

19:15.991 --> 19:18.495
That comes out of my paycheck
if you take it.

19:18.576 --> 19:20.787
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

19:20.913 --> 19:23.165
Well, I can't in all good conscience
take that, then.

19:23.291 --> 19:25.667
- Oh, good. Thank you. Thank you, that's...
- Yeah. Yeah.

19:25.793 --> 19:27.628
No. I'm a working man myself.

19:27.753 --> 19:28.795
- No. It's tough out there.
- Yeah.

19:28.879 --> 19:29.880
You know, you can't...

19:30.005 --> 19:32.548
- You got to find a way.
- It's tough, it is.

19:32.674 --> 19:35.469
All right. Well, can you stop this thing
so we can get off?

19:35.594 --> 19:38.013
No. I mean, I'd love to.

19:38.097 --> 19:40.475
But it stops at the predesignated stops.

19:40.558 --> 19:43.186
You know, I don't have control,
you know, over that.

19:43.311 --> 19:44.561
- Oh.
- That's the engineer who does that stuff.

19:44.688 --> 19:45.688
Well, how...

19:45.813 --> 19:47.899
Well, how much are our tickets?

19:48.025 --> 19:50.650
Well, for this, this is a first-class cabin.

19:50.776 --> 19:51.986
It's 25 bucks.

19:52.196 --> 19:54.197
Wow! And we're the robbers.

19:54.824 --> 19:57.910
- Okay. How much is coach?
- $12 for coach.

19:58.327 --> 19:59.286
Well, he's a senior...

19:59.411 --> 20:02.540
You know what? That's fine.
Just give me two coach tickets.

20:03.247 --> 20:04.457
All right, thank you.

20:04.540 --> 20:06.836
<i>Oh, wow! When did Mamma Mia!
Come to the Oakdale?</i>

20:06.919 --> 20:08.838
Oh, yeah. What... Just a week ago, I think.

20:08.919 --> 20:11.091
Oh, wow! We should go. Do you want to...

20:11.216 --> 20:12.425
<i>You want to go see Mamma Mia?</i>

20:12.550 --> 20:15.383
Peter, could I speak to you
over by the door?

20:17.972 --> 20:19.307
Good as new.

20:20.183 --> 20:21.683
Oh, come on!

20:24.185 --> 20:25.228
I give up.

20:25.354 --> 20:27.854
We're gonna be
lower middle-class Americans forever.

20:27.980 --> 20:29.733
A fate worse than death.

20:29.858 --> 20:31.821
Seriously, we may as well just be dead.

20:31.904 --> 20:33.865
You know what, Peter? That's not true.

20:33.947 --> 20:36.532
In the time we've spent together,
I've learned something.

20:36.656 --> 20:39.369
When you're rich,
you don't own your possessions,

20:39.453 --> 20:41.161
your possessions own you.

20:41.244 --> 20:42.789
Oh, Carter, darling!

20:42.913 --> 20:44.374
Babs, sweetheart!

20:44.500 --> 20:46.168
Honey, we're rich again.

20:46.295 --> 20:48.669
I divorced Ted Turner
and took half his money.

20:48.752 --> 20:50.380
<i>We own half of CNN.</i>

20:51.591 --> 20:53.341
<i>- And TNT.
- Neat!</i>

20:53.425 --> 20:56.219
- All right, buddy, we did it! We're rich!
- "We"?

20:56.344 --> 20:57.930
Go to hell, you fat peasant!

20:58.056 --> 20:59.388
Crap!

20:59.515 --> 21:02.559
Peter, listen to me. Money doesn't matter.

21:02.852 --> 21:05.937
10 years ago Daddy offered
to give us $10 million,

21:06.062 --> 21:07.397
and I turned it down.

21:07.523 --> 21:08.565
- What?
- Yes.

21:08.690 --> 21:10.234
And I'll always turn it down

21:10.360 --> 21:12.903
because money
just complicates everything.

21:13.028 --> 21:15.948
We don't need money
because we have each other.

21:16.115 --> 21:18.908
Happiness isn't about
buying expensive things,

21:19.035 --> 21:20.912
it's about being together.

21:21.287 --> 21:24.084
It's not about taking expensive trips.

21:24.167 --> 21:27.544
It's about holding each other
during a thunderstorm.

21:27.626 --> 21:30.171
And we have that kind of happiness, Peter.

21:30.296 --> 21:33.424
Real happiness
because we have each other.

21:33.800 --> 21:35.218
Yeah.

21:35.219 --> 22:36.219
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru